WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.960
The story goes that the
first temple to stand at

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:05.450
the site in the image
was built by a race of

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:07.430
little people known as
the Menehune.

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:11.530
Thousands of men were
needed to construct this

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:12.910
temple. Thousands of
them.

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:16.860
And it took one night,
according to legend.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:21.410
Studies suggest that in
the 12th century the

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:24.470
temple is rebuilt and
its walls heightened to

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:29.920
30ft. It is dedicated to
the God ku a deity who

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:33.250
shapeshifts between
human and shark form and

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:35.170
is known as the eater of
islands.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.750
He is a particularly
fearsome God.

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:40.210
He's the God of war.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:44.260
Ku was probably the most
important of these

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:47.440
Hawaiian gods and only
the King.

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:50.500
The priesthood and the
highest nobles were

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:51.850
allowed access to the
temple.

